	"_comment": "Swipe direction to configuration slot, replayed by the macOS geometry (modules/gestures/geometry.lua) and the Linux evdev decoder (modules/gestures/mt_decoder.lua), which both classify through _shared/lua/gestures/direction.lua. Angles use the screen convention both drivers classify in: 0 is right and 90 is down, so y grows downward. Units differ per driver, so each consumer scales the unit vector to a multiple of its own swipe threshold: travel 'swipe' is four times the threshold, travel 'short' a quarter of it, which is no swipe at all (slot null). A slot is swipe_<fingers>_<direction>, horizontal part first for a diagonal, and must be declared in _shared/modules/actions/actions.toml. boundary_vectors pin the classifier itself in normalised units, a swipe minimum of 1 and the boundary_rule diagonal minimum: travel is Manhattan (|dx| + |dy|), a swipe within 25 degrees of an axis is straight (both boundaries inclusive), a diagonal needs the diagonal minimum and otherwise takes its dominant axis, horizontal on a tie. Each consumer multiplies dx and dy by its own swipe minimum.",
